 "lead_paragraphs": [
  {
   "label": {
    "en": "CAPITAL RETURNS:",
    "zh": "现金分配："
   },
   "text": {
    "en": "FY12-25 OCF $105.8B less capex $72.5B left **$33.3B FCF**. Dividends **$19.1B (57%)**; buybacks **$7.6B (23%)**; acquisitions **$4.4B** (Encino). Most of the payout came after 2021: **$15.4B** of dividends in FY21-25.",
    "zh": "FY12-25 OCF $105.8B 减资本开支 $72.5B，得 **FCF $33.3B**。股息 **$19.1B（57%）**；回购 **$7.6B（23%）**；收购 **$4.4B**（Encino）。分配主要发生在 2021 年后：FY21-25 股息 **$15.4B**。"
   }
  },
  {
   "label": {
    "en": "NET SHARES:",
    "zh": "净股数变化："
   },
   "text": {
    "en": "Split-adjusted shares FY11 532M to FY25 546M (**+2.6%**; Yates merger 2016). Buybacks since FY23 cut the count from 587M (FY22) to 546M, **down 7.0%**.",
    "zh": "拆股调整后股数由 FY11 的 532M 增至 FY25 的 546M（**+2.6%**；2016 年合并 Yates）。FY23 起回购使股数由 587M（FY22）降至 546M，**减少 7.0%**。"
   }
  }
 ],
 "commentary": [
  {
   "headline": {
    "en": "A price-taker with a low-cost base.",
    "zh": "价格接受者，但成本低。"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Operating income swung from -$6.7B (2015) to +$10.0B (2022) with oil prices. What EOG controls is cost: cash cost held at $10.1-10.5/Boe through FY21-25, including the 2022 inflation spike.",
    "zh": "营业利润随油价从 -$6.7B（2015）摆动到 +$10.0B（2022）。EOG 能控制的是成本：FY21-25 现金成本保持在 $10.1-10.5/桶油当量，2022 年通胀高峰也未失控。"
   }
  },
  {
   "headline": {
    "en": "FCF arrived only after 2017.",
    "zh": "FCF 在 2017 年后才出现。"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "FY11-16 capex exceeded OCF in four of six years. Since FY18 FCF has been positive every year, peaking at $6.8B in FY24, as capex fell from ~75% of OCF (FY18-19) to 41-61% (FY21-25).",
    "zh": "FY11-16 六年中有四年资本开支超过 OCF。FY18 起 FCF 每年为正，FY24 峰值 $6.8B；资本开支占 OCF 由 FY18-19 的约 75% 降至 FY21-25 的 41-61%。"
   }
  },
  {
   "headline": {
    "en": "Payouts follow the cycle.",
    "zh": "分配跟随周期。"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Dividends jumped to $5.1B in FY22 with special payouts, then the mix shifted to buybacks ($3.2B in FY24, $2.6B in FY25). In FY25 payouts were 120% of FCF as prices fell. If oil falls back toward my $70 mid-cycle deck, FCF and buybacks shrink together; the base dividend is the part to watch.",
    "zh": "FY22 含特别股息，股息升至 $5.1B；之后转向回购（FY24 $3.2B，FY25 $2.6B）。FY25 油价回落，分配达到 FCF 的 120%。若油价回到我假设的 $70 中周期水平，FCF 与回购会一起缩小；应关注的是基础股息。"
   }
  },
  {
   "headline": {
    "en": "Gas is the new growth line.",
    "zh": "天然气是新的增长线。"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Gas output rose from 1,948 MMcf/d (FY24) to 3,055 (1H26) after the $4.45B Encino (Utica) deal; gas revenue +80% in FY25. That adds Henry Hub exposure as LNG exports grow.",
    "zh": "收购 Encino（Utica，$44.5 亿）后，天然气产量由 FY24 的 19.48 亿立方英尺/日升至 2026年上半年 30.55 亿；FY25 天然气收入 +80%。随着 LNG 出口增长，Henry Hub 敞口加大。"
   }
  },
  {
   "headline": {
    "en": "The balance sheet is a buffer.",
    "zh": "资产负债表是缓冲。"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Net debt/EBITDA was below zero in FY22-24 and only 0.49x after Encino (0.23x TTM). That lets EOG keep paying through a downturn without cutting the base dividend, and leaves room for another bolt-on deal.",
    "zh": "FY22-24 净债务/EBITDA 为负，收购 Encino 后也仅 0.49 倍（TTM 0.23 倍）。这让 EOG 在下行期也能维持基础股息，并为再做一笔补强收购留出空间。"
   }
  },
  {
   "headline": {
    "en": "The price deck decides the value.",
    "zh": "价格假设决定估值。"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Base $146.17 (WACC 8.6%, g 1.5%, beta 0.9) assumes WTI fades from $87 (2026) to $70 by 2030; TV is 76% of EV. At $155.47 that is -6%. Bear $73 (WTI $58) and bull $231 (WTI $85-95) show the range.",
    "zh": "基准价值 $146.17（WACC 8.6%，g 1.5%，beta 0.9）假设 WTI 由 2026 年的 $87 回落到 2030 年的 $70；终值占 EV 76%。按 $155.47 计为 -6%。悲观 $73（WTI $58）、乐观 $231（WTI $85-95）显示了区间之宽。"
   }
  }
 ],
